|~ What is declared under `::builtin`, the descriptor of a
   primitive: the refusals of the kernel no reader reaches by a query,
   the table of primitives, the tree the evaluator does not know, the
   session, the printer and the sources of the root. ~|

:builtin/BuiltinPayloadNotMapError
  |~~ `::builtin` holds the fields of a declaration as a map,
      `::builtin{:impl …}`; a payload of another kind is refused.

      ~(
        ::builtin"hello"
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::builtin/BuiltinPayloadNotMapError ::string]
       )
      ~(
        ::builtin[1 2 3]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::builtin/BuiltinPayloadNotMapError ::vec]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/UnknownAstNodeTypeError
  |~~ The evaluator met a node of the parser's tree it has no rule for:
      a defect of the runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/UnknownCombinatorKindError
  |~~ The evaluator met a combinator it has no rule for: a defect of the
      runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/PrimitiveKeyAlreadyBoundError
  |~~ Two files of the runtime bound one primitive name, a defect of
      the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/ThrowSiteSpecAlreadyRecordedError
  |~~ Two sites of the runtime declared one refusal under one name, a
      defect of the runtime found as it loads: the name is the identity
      the page and the `spec` of the refusal read, so one site would
      speak for both.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/PrimitiveKeyNotStringError
  |~~ A file of the runtime bound a primitive under a name that is no
      string, a defect of the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/PrimitiveKeyUnboundError
  |~~ The `:impl` of a declaration names a primitive no file of the
      runtime bound: a verb or a kind declared by a source whose
      implementation was not handed with it.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/PrimitiveRegistrySealedError
  |~~ The table of primitives is sealed when the bootstrap completes,
      and a primitive bound after it is refused.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/NumberNotFiniteLeakedToPrintError
  |~~ A number of qlang is a finite double. Source cannot mint an
      infinity or a NaN — the parser refuses the literal and every
      arithmetic site answers an error of its domain — so this tag
      reports a value a host installed. The print and the JSON of the
      boundary are where such a value shows: the print would be
      `Infinity`, which no literal reads back, and JSON would write
      `null`. `:actualValue` holds the magnitude as a string, the one
      form that prints.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/BootstrapSourceMissingError
  |~~ A source of the language resolved to nothing, so the root lacks
      what it declares; `:uri` names the source. The host maps the source
      in the imports of its package or in the import map of a browser, or
      hands the runtime a locator of its own.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/RootSourceNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A source of the root answered an error, so its declarations stay
      out of the root; `:uri` names the source and `:tagName` what it
      answered, `::bind/BindNameDeclaredTwiceError` for a name the root
      already holds, a refusal under a second address among them.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/RootImplNamesNoVerbError
  |~~ A host handed an implementation beside a source of the root for a
      name the source declares as no verb: an implementation is the
      primitive of a verb the source declares. `:uri` names the source
      and `:implName` the name.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:builtin/SourceLoadError
  |~~ The platform resolved a `#qlang/<ns>` logical name to a path or
      URL the host could not read. The descriptor carries `:host`
      (`:node` / `:web`), `:logicalName`, `:sourceLocation`, and either
      the underlying `:cause` or the HTTP `:status`. A host that ships
      its own catalog hands the runtime a locator of the sources of the
      language and never reaches the platform loader.
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
